  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and Development for Elimination of NTDs (ENDPOINT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Neglected Tropical Diseases (NTDs) adversely affect the health and economic prosperity of the most vulnerable in global society, yet many have the potential to be eradicated or eliminated as a public health problem. For this to be achieved, the World Health Organisation recognises that innovations in new treatment interventions, better diagnostics, and synergistic control measures to suppress the insects which spread NTDs between people are urgently required. The WHO has formulated a roadmap to NTD elimination with specific targets set by 2030. Responding to this policy initiative, ENDPOINT is a multidisciplinary international product development partnership co-ordinated by The Liverpool School of Tropical Medicine Centre for Drugs &amp; Diagnostics.</narrative>
  </description>
